# Implementation Plan - PehchaanAI Blockchain Verification Module

Implement an end-to-end, tamper-evident Blockchain Verification module for PehchaanAI following the completed Verification Result flow:
```
Verification Result
→ Generate Verification Record
→ Generate SHA-256 Hash
→ Store verification hash on blockchain (or record as Pending/Config Required if RPC offline)
→ Receive Transaction/Block ID
→ Verify hash integrity
→ Display Blockchain Verification Status
→ Maintain immutable audit trail
```

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Strict Security & Zero Fake Blockchain Data Policy:**
> 1. **No PII On-Chain**: In strict compliance with privacy standards, Aadhaar/Passport/PAN numbers, raw photos, biometric images, or sensitive personal data will **never** be stored on the blockchain. Only deterministic SHA-256 hashes and minimal non-sensitive metadata (`documentId` reference, `documentType`, `verificationStatus`, `riskScore`, `timestamp`) will be anchored.
> 2. **No Fake Transactions**: In accordance with Requirement 11 & 21, if no live Ethereum/EVM RPC node or testnet is configured, the system will explicitly report **`Not Connected`** / **`Configuration Required`** and set `txHash: null` / `blockNumber: null`. It will never generate counterfeit tx hashes or claim simulated blocks are mined on a real blockchain.
> 3. **Live EVM Ready**: A clean abstraction service with environment variables (`BLOCKCHAIN_PROVIDER_URL`, `BLOCKCHAIN_CONTRACT_ADDRESS`, `BLOCKCHAIN_PRIVATE_KEY`, `BLOCKCHAIN_NETWORK_NAME`) and a production-ready Solidity registry contract (`DocumentVerificationRegistry.sol`) will be provided so any EVM chain (Sepolia, Hardhat, Ganache, Polygon) can be connected at any time.

