  - `riskScore`: Number
  - `timestamp`: Date
  - `recordHash`: String (SHA-256 digest)
  - `canonicalPayload`: String (transparent proof string)
  - `blockchainStatus`: String ('Verified', 'Pending', 'Failed', 'Configuration Required')
  - `txHash`: String (null if not anchored)
  - `blockNumber`: Number (null if not anchored)
  - `networkName`: String
  - `officerBadge`: String
  - `auditTrail`: Array of events:
    - `{ action, timestamp, details, performedBy }`

#### [NEW] [`backend/src/routes/blockchainRoutes.js`](file:///c:/Users/ritik/OneDrive/Desktop/PehchaanAI/backend/src/routes/blockchainRoutes.js)
- Express router mounted at `/api/blockchain`:
  - `GET /status`: Combines Python RPC connection status + MongoDB metrics (total records, verified records, latest block).
  - `POST /record`: Accepts verification result, calls Python service for SHA-256 and anchoring, saves to MongoDB with initial audit log entry.
  - `GET /records`: Returns list of records with optional filter/search.
  - `GET /record/:documentId`: Fetches a single record by document ID or case ID.
  - `POST /verify-integrity`: Recalculates hash, verifies integrity against MongoDB/blockchain, appends audit log entry (`INTEGRITY_VERIFIED` or `INTEGRITY_FAILED`).

